#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fort Galgs: a front end for fortctl's CPU reservation.

This is a front end. Every change to the machine belongs to fortctl, which
this program shells out to; if a change fails, its own words are what the
user sees. The live picture reads /proc/stat and cgroup cpu.stat directly,
because those are read-only and cheap.

Run with --self-test to build every page and draw every state once, or with
--snapshot <png> to draw the chip from live load. --time-scale <x> runs the
valley's clock x times faster than real time, to watch the seasons turn.
--almanac <years> [--seed N] runs a fresh valley headless and prints a row
for every season. --siege <minutes> [--seed N] runs a fresh siege headless
and prints a row for every minute: the redcoats sent, shot, at the wall and
killed by the gun, and the calls for it; the boats, which need the river's
drawn course, are left out. The valley itself is kept in
$XDG_STATE_HOME/fort-galgs/world.json between runs.
"""

